"""Invented fantasy / sci-fi names with no real-world romanisation system. Original prose."""

PASSAGES = [
("inv01", """[[Vael'thar|p|inv]] drew his blade beneath the twin moons of [[Ixomir|l|inv]]. The [[Ashen Concord|o|inv]] had marched for nine days, and the [[Concordat|t|ali]], as the soldiers called their commander, was weary. “[[Vael'thar|p|inv]],” said [[Oryn Dask|p|inv]], “the [[Glass Throne|i]] is not worth the ruin.” “Nothing is.” Behind them a horn sounded from the walls of [[Ixomir|l|inv]]. The old captain, called [[Dask|p|inv]] by his friends and [[Captain Oryn|p|tit]] by his men, readied the standard."""),
("inv02", """The spire of [[Quel-Anor|l|inv]] was empty. [[Nyssa Thorne|p|inv]] climbed it anyway, and the [[Warden|t]] of the spire watched from a window. “[[Thorne|p|inv]],” he said, “you carry the [[Silver Lathe|i|inv]]?” “I do.” “Then you are the one the [[Order of Quiet Hands|o|inv]] foretold.” She shrugged. Sentences like that always meant trouble. Hope, she thought, was a fine sentiment for people with fewer enemies. Below, [[Brother Calum|p|tit]] sang an old dirge to the stones."""),
("inv03", """“Will you come?” asked [[Zaeli|p|inv]], and the stranger, [[Kor Veshtan|p|inv]], paused. Everyone in the harbour called him [[Will|p|wl]], because he never said no. [[Kor|p|inv]] was his true name, and [[Veshtan|p|inv]] his family's. Their ship, the [[Dusk Marten|i|inv]], tugged at its rope. The [[harbourmaster|t]] of [[Pellam Quay|l|inv]] waved them off, and a flock of gulls rose over the [[Brass Guild|o|inv]] warehouse. “[[Zaeli|p|inv]],” said [[Will|p|wl]], “cast off.”"""),
("inv04", """Two tribes shared the salt flats of [[Orrovan|l|inv]], and each had a [[chieftain|t|sh]]. The [[chieftain|t|sh]] of the [[Sand Hawks|o|inv]] was named [[Brak Uum|p|inv]]. The [[chieftain|t|sh]] of the [[Red Herons|o|inv]] was named [[Sethra Quill|p|inv]]. Neither would sit first. “[[Brak|p|inv]],” murmured an elder, “the water-bearers wait.” “Let [[Quill|p|inv]] begin.” “Let the [[Hawk|t|ali]] begin,” she answered, meaning him. Wind blew grit across the tents. The sacred bowl, [[Mother of Rain|i]], waited between them, empty."""),
("inv05", """A city and its first king shared one name, which caused no end of confusion. The scholars at the [[Library of Ashmoor|l]] wrote [[King Ixomir|p|tit]] for the man and [[Ixomir|l|inv]] for the place. “[[Archivist Pell|p|tit]],” said a student, “which [[Ixomir|l|inv]] is in the first scroll?” “Both,” said [[Pell|p|inv]]. “Neither.” The [[Scroll of Seven Doors|i]] smelled of dust and oil. A bell rang from the [[Quiet Tower|l]], and the students gathered their notes."""),
("inv06", """Grace was a virtue in [[Merrowdeep|l|inv]], and a name as well. [[Grace Ilmarin|p|wl]] bowed at the temple of the [[Tidal Choir|o|inv]]. “[[Lady Ilmarin|p|tit]],” said the cantor, “the sea is calling.” “It always is.” People called her [[Grace|p|wl]], or [[Ilmarin|p|inv]], or [[the Pearl Matron|t|ali]]; each meant the same patient woman. Her lantern, [[Mourning Star|i]], never lit by itself. Beyond the harbour, the black kelp rolled in slow waves."""),
("inv07", """“[[Hunter|p|si]], wake.” [[Hunter Rhoss|p|wl]] opened his eyes in the cold of the ship [[Argent Wake|l|inv]]. He had been a bounty man on [[Kellan Prime|l|inv]], and the crew still called him [[Hunter|p|wl]], though the [[Provost|t]] used his surname. “[[Rhoss|p|inv]],” said the [[Provost|t]], “the [[Helix Authority|o|inv]] has issued a warrant.” “Naturally.” He reached for the pistol named [[Quiet Debt|i|inv]]. Outside, the stars wheeled past the hull like cold coins."""),
("inv08", """[[Maelis|p|inv]] and [[Maelor|p|inv]] were twins born under the same eclipse. The [[Seer of Embers|t|ali]] had warned the court: one would be [[Queen|t|sh]], the other [[Queen|t|sh]], and the realm would split. “[[Maelis|p|inv]],” whispered the nurse, “you are the elder.” “And [[Maelor|p|inv]]?” “The cleverer.” In the great hall of [[Karthuun|l|inv]], the [[Court of Veils|o|inv]] gathered in grey silks. The two girls clasped hands. Between them hung the crown called [[Dawnthorn|i|inv]]."""),
("inv09", """[[Rain|p|si]] was an unusual name for a dwarf, but [[Rain Hammerfell|p|wl]] bore it proudly. “[[Hammerfell|p|inv]]!” called the foreman, [[Boss Tuck|p|tit]]. “The forge at [[Deepdelve|l|inv]] is cold!” “Then light it, [[Tuck|p|inv]].” The [[Stonebeard Clan|o|inv]] sent a messenger. “[[Rain-of-the-Hammer|p|ali]],” he said, using the old style, “your [[clan head|t]] requests you.” She wiped her hands. The anvil, [[Old Mother|i]], rang with a note like laughter, and the cavern answered."""),
("inv10", """[[Tessaly|p|inv]] kept the lighthouse of [[Mirren Point|l|inv]], and the sailors called her [[the Lamp Keeper|t|ali]]. Her real name, [[Tessaly Vane|p|inv]], appeared only on the charts. “[[Vane|p|inv]]!” cried the captain of the [[Sable Heron|i|inv]], a ship battered by storm. “Light the beacon!” “It is lit,” she said. A moment later the wind snapped the shutters, and [[Tessaly|p|inv]] smiled. Somewhere above, the [[Tidewatch League|o|inv]] had struck its colours and gone home, forgetting her."""),
("inv11", """The dragon had three names. The villagers of [[Hollowmere|l|inv]] said [[Skarn|p|inv]]; the scholars at the [[Academy of Flame|o|inv]] said [[Skarnathyx|p|inv]]; the knights said [[the Grey Tyrant|t|ali]]. “Which is correct?” asked [[Sir Aldous|p|tit]]. “All.” In the cave mouth, a bell hung from a chain: the [[Bell of Ruin|i]]. The old [[knight-commander|t]] struck it once. A long, slow breath answered from the dark, and the villagers, far below, stopped their work and bowed."""),
("inv12", """[[Pip|p|wl]] and [[Joy|p|wl]] were the two smallest scouts of the [[Lantern Company|o|inv]], and the only ones the [[captain|t]] trusted with keys. “[[Pip|p|wl]],” said [[Joy|p|wl]], “are we lost?” “Never.” They stood in the ruined plaza of [[Orsellin|l|inv]], where a statue of [[Lord Haskell|p|tit]] had lost its head. [[Sergeant Mose|p|tit]] called from the rear: “Scouts! The [[Moth Gate|l|inv]] is open!” Neither scout moved. The key, [[Pale Truth|i|inv]], hung warm against [[Pip|p|wl]]'s chest."""),
("inv13", """Sentry [[Dovrin|p|inv]] reported to [[Commander Eleth|p|tit]] at dawn. “[[Eleth|p|inv]],” he said, “the [[Ninth Fleet|o]] has not returned.” The commander nodded. In the war room of [[Station Calyx|l|inv]], the map of the [[Veiled Sector|l|inv]] glowed. “And the [[Vice-Admiral|t]]?” “Missing.” “[[Dovrin|p|inv]], send for [[Doctor Ishka|p|tit]].” The doctor arrived, carrying the [[Sigil of Nine Wounds|i|inv]], the only proof that the fleet had ever reached the [[Maw|l|inv]]. Nobody liked that proof."""),
("inv14", """In the forest of [[Eldrasil|l|inv]], two druids answered to [[Greywalker|t|sh]]. One was [[Aenwyn Thistle|p|inv]]; the other [[Corvus Ash|p|inv]]. When a lost child asked, “[[Greywalker|t|sh]], where is the road?”, both said, “Follow me.” The [[Circle of Moss|o|inv]] had never resolved the problem. [[Aenwyn|p|inv]] favoured the staff [[Rootsong|i|inv]]; [[Corvus|p|inv]] kept a horn named [[Thornwhisper|i|inv]]. The child, [[Mina|p]], trailed behind, delighted by the confusion and sure she was in no danger."""),
("inv15", """[[Zhorel|p|inv]], [[Zhorell|p|inv]], and [[Jorel|p|inv]] were the same man: a smuggler on [[Thessen Dock|l|inv]], whose name changed with each port's accent. “[[Captain Zhorel|p|tit]],” said the pilot. “[[Mister Jorel|p|tit]],” said the customs man. “[[Old Z|p|ali]],” said his crew. The [[Salt Syndicate|o|inv]] wanted a word. He ignored it. In his coat pocket lay a small iron whistle, [[Thrush Call|i|inv]], that could summon any ship in the harbour. He stroked it, and smiled at the wet horizon."""),
]
